5. IDOR vs BOLA?


✅ IDOR = A specific type of access control vulnerability where an attacker manipulates an object identifier (e.g., user ID, account number) to access unauthorized data.

✅ BOLA = A broader authorization issue where the application/API fails to verify whether the user is allowed to access a particular object.


