4. In the application there was search field then how explain reflected Xss and DOM Xss 

I verify whether the payload is reflected in the server response. If the server returns my unsanitized input and the browser executes it,
I classify it as Reflected XSS.

If I enter an XSS payload into a search field, I first inspect the HTTP response in Burp Suite. If the payload is reflected by the server and executes,
it is Reflected XSS. If the payload is not present in the response but executes because client-side JavaScript reads user input and inserts it into 
the DOM using unsafe methods like innerHTML, then it is DOM XSS.

